"Quick Start Details" = "MicLock configures the microphone; a voice input method turns speech into text. Choose one from Voice Input Recommendations if you have not installed one.\n\n1. Under Configure Microphone, choose your built-in microphone and enable Automatic Lock. Locking starts off on a new installation.\n\n2. Open your voice input method, choose System Default for its microphone if that setting is available, and try a sentence in a text field. Your headphones can keep playing audio.\n\n3. Use the top menu bar icon to configure or pause. Close Status and Settings to keep MicLock running. Maintenance and temporary input switching are under More.\n\nMicLock waits if the target disconnects. You can pause or quit anytime. It does not record audio or change recognition algorithms.";
"Sharing Text" = "Voice input gets worse when headphones connect? Check whether macOS switched the microphone. MicLock keeps your preferred microphone as the system default input. Choose System Default in your voice app. No audio recording. Updates and feedback connect only when you choose them. Downloads and instructions: https://ecnkfnba0c1r.feishuapp.com/app/app_17ftjhzb3vs";

